  "yt_description": "Under the hood, Git is a simple key-value store.\n\n• You hand Git content, it returns a 40-character SHA-1 key\n• The key is a hash of a small header plus the content\n• Objects live in .git/objects: first 2 characters are the folder, the other 38 the file name\n• blob = file content, tree = names + pointers, commit = one tree + parent + message\n• Try it: git cat-file -p <hash>\n\n#git #programming #softwareengineering #developers #coding",
  "ig_caption": "Git is secretly just a key-value store. 🗝️\n\n📦 Hand it content, get back a 40-character key\n🔐 Key = SHA-1 of a small header + your content\n📁 Stored in .git/objects (2 chars folder, 38 chars file)\n🌳 blob = content, tree = names, commit = tree + parent + message\n\nTry: git cat-file -p <hash>\n\nFollow @stackshade for more.\n\nVoiceover is AI-generated. Source: Pro Git, Git Internals.",
